Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["A Working Tour of the Symmetry Functions", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"bc5c84ba-5242-4a4d-b571-bfc05938f3c7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This tutorial walks through every function in ",
 StyleBox["Wolfram`TensorNetworks`Symmetry`", "Code"],
 " in the order a tensor-network practitioner meets them. After it you can \
(i) decide whether a partition or a tableau is the right object for a \
problem, (ii) predict the size of every block of a symmetry-resolved tensor \
in closed form, and (iii) project a TN tensor onto the \
irreducible-representation subspace it physically belongs to. Every claim is \
paired with a Wolfram Language cell; nothing is asserted without being \
computed."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a11d811a-9e64-437d-bff4-b240a3a4b40b"],

Cell["\<\
The arc starts at two indistinguishable particles and walks up the rank, \
picking up one Symmetry function per step. By the end all sixteen exported \
functions appear at least once on a tensor with a tensor-network reason to \
exist.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"24b5ecf0-a4ed-4b4f-9092-503e03cc0b42"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Inventory", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"8904dfa1-5eec-4e37-81ae-4c0e3dad8dee"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Symmetry layer exports sixteen symbols. Six handle the ",
 StyleBox["combinatorics",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " of Young diagrams. Two are typed ",
 StyleBox["accessors",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " for the row and column structure of a tableau. Six are ",
 StyleBox["dimensions",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " of the irreducible-representation blocks, split between the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["S", "n"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1e7c77fd-8089-483a-be75-b5104a5c948b"],
 " side (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"dim", " ", 
    SubscriptBox["V", "\[Lambda]"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"0ef6d2b4-1b4c-407e-a49d-7faf5034e8c4"],
 ") and the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"G", " ", "L", "(", "d", ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"05344adf-cdcc-42c0-842b-fb9102066757"],
 " side (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"dim", " ", 
    SubscriptBox["W", "\[Lambda]"], "(", "d", ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"17f4e336-0442-4447-9122-679b04e1adb4"],
 "). Two are ",
 StyleBox["tensor actions",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " that produce a tensor in a chosen symmetry class."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0818279a-f032-4ca1-a9ed-e5ab7194ab82"],

