 CellLabel->
  "Out[191]=",ExpressionUUID->"20bef904-f358-4e83-8ee0-8a0bf5cb06db"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Bianchi appears at position 1; the second three-term identity is its image \
under the pair-swap-plus-(34)-antisym relations already in the two-term \
sweep. The multi-term constraint that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"Symmetrize", "paclet:ref/Symmetrize"},
   "RefLink"]], "Text",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "ed84a307-f3c1-4b47-af35-3f251e2766d4"],
 " could not reach has been generated from the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", " ", "2", ",", "2", " ", "}"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"136be9b7-2c72-485a-9db5-87e9357e3cdc"],
 " Young projector itself, not assumed, not looked up."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cad4f2a7-da1e-4a70-8a2d-6997e6ee5208"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For completeness, point-check the four classical Riemann identities on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["R", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "446698b3-7fa0-43f4-9057-38674da9bf41"],
 " directly (redundant now, since each is in the discovered list)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7a4f8d49-3f28-4c42-9adc-d193e4ae2be1"],

